  "body": "The manifest harness rejected harmless `# Requires ...` comments and could admit uppercase `#REQUIRES` directives under Turkish/Azeri cultures. Read `ScriptBlockAst.ScriptRequirements` before extracting data or importing a module, validating the actual PowerShell 5.1/7 metadata members and types. Preserve the existing AST and schema guards.\n\nFixes the code defect tracked by #1295; corrective Packet #1296, Mission #1238. Debt stays open until verified land. Product diff: one harness file, +66/-2. Manifest, runtime modules, S1/S2 tests and publication files are unchanged.\n\nValidation on H2 `15ad82f56924a0ccc99833ec73eec078ce00b726`:\n\n- Linux lifecycle selftest 1777/1777; strict manifest 184/184; Ruff delta 0 against the unchanged baseline.\n- Native PowerShell 5.1 and 7: normal 7/7, CX parent 12/12 and S2 normal 26/26 on each runtime; 57 meaningful requirement rejections before import across the culture matrix, plus historical AST, baseline reproduction and guard-only rollback controls.\n- Six literal controls pass PM01 and fail PM02 with exactly `VALUE[RootModule]`, with no runtime children. They are schema-negative controls, not full-suite positives or semantic kills.\n- Independent full-source audit passed: 1,876 native source files, 95 observations and matching owned ledger rows; source export hashes before/after match committed B/H2 bytes. Native inputs are scoped Git-blob exports, not a full native Git checkout. Original operator failures remain recorded.\n\nNo Windows CI or full Windows mutant CI, per owner instruction; focused native tests ran. No runtime activation or LIVE deployment.\n\nThis PR remains draft. CI, exact-head connector and complete-source CI audit have passed. Owner human approval on both axes is recorded: https://github.com/ducthangho/tra-luat/pull/1301#issuecomment-6736642798. Final gate readbacks, Ready/automatic review and normal merge/postmerge evidence remain required. The old H4 human audit and waiver do not apply to H2.\n\nOffline independent review: https://github.com/ducthangho/tra-luat/issues/1296#issuecomment-6735182321; v2 receipt: `f16c9dbc69809008ea4966516463ff6aa5a7c359:ops/reviews/wp1296-r3-review1.receipt.yaml`. Both axes approve, no open findings; same-provider approval, sensitive assurance HOLD.\n\n\nCI update:23/23Ubuntu jobs,24/24checks, four anchors/full-source AUX5 and exact-H2 Draft connector completed. [Evidence](https://github.com/ducthangho/tra-luat/blob/ab08513724c1c3f51095f153051fe9b92379e781/ops/checkpoints/wp1296-r3/PRCI/final-evidence-index.json); [human audit bundle](https://github.com/ducthangho/tra-luat/blob/ab08513724c1c3f51095f153051fe9b92379e781/ops/checkpoints/wp1296-r3/human-audit-H2/HUMAN-AUDIT.md). Human approval on exact H2 has now been received and published; keep draft until final readiness gates are satisfied.\n\n\nOwner approval update: [both-axis human verdict](https://github.com/ducthangho/tra-luat/pull/1301#issuecomment-6736642798), v2 receipt validated at `5d77077f8bf1f099a5260b987cf9c38645c0eb16`. This is supplemental exact-H2 assurance; no backdating or inheritance of old H4 audit. PR has not been marked Ready or merged by this publication.\n",
